                "value": "The Dongnae-eupseong History Festival showcases a historical reenactment of a fierce battle, where Song Sang-hyeon, the national war hero, and the townspeople of Dongnae-eupseong fought in unity to protect the Dongnae-eupseong Fortress during the Japanese invasion of Korea in 1592. It also provides participants with an opportunity to experience life in the past, and includes an ancient marketplace. It is held in the North Gate area of Dongrae-eupseong during every second week of October. It is a representative historical festival that has been recognized by the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism in 2014, 2015, 2016 and 2018.",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "DateTimeOriginal": {
                "value": "2017-10-20 19:41:16",
